  set:  # bbe5
    description: "## Origin\n\nFiled per discussion surrounding WI-votut. See sister item `WI-mifif` (Django) — the first-framework PR.\n\n## Gap\n\n`hypergumbo run` on a Laravel app produces no `renders` edge connecting a controller method to its Blade template. The implicit `view('users.show', $data)` → `resources/views/users/show.blade.php` relationship is not captured.\n\n## Laravel convention to model\n\n- **Action detection**: methods on classes that extend `Illuminate\\Routing\\Controller` or `App\\Http\\Controllers\\Controller` (the app's base controller, which itself extends Illuminate's).\n- **View name source**: the **string argument** to a `view(...)` helper call (or `View::make(...)` facade). Like Spring, this is explicit, not method-name-based.\n  - `view('users.show', $data)` → `resources/views/users/show.blade.php` (dots = directory separators).\n  - `view('users.show')` (no second arg) → same.\n  - `View::make('users.show')` → same.\n- **Template path derivation**: replace dots with `/` in the view name; resolve under `resources/views/`.\n- **Extensions**: `.blade.php` (Blade — primary), `.php` (raw PHP fallback).\n\n## Strategy alignment with shared core\n\nThis linker uses the **explicit-string strategy** exposed by the shared core (assuming WI-mifif lands both strategy hooks per its scope; if not, this PR extracts the explicit-string strategy as its own contribution).\n\n## Coordination with WI-hogik (Spring MVC)\n\nSpring and Laravel share the explicit-string strategy. Neither has an `isbefore` on the other; whichever lands first does the actual extraction work (if WI-mifif didn't already set it up), the second is a thin port. Spring detects string-return-value of an annotated method; Laravel detects string-argument of a `view()`/`View::make()` call. Different per-language detection variants, same underlying strategy.\n\n## Build order\n\nBlocked on WI-mifif merging (shared core extraction).\n\n## Analyzer pre-req\n\nConfirm before scheduling: the PHP analyzer correctly extracts class-extends relationships AND string-arg-of-function-call (specifically `view('...')`, `View::make('...')`). Sibling lang-mainstream/lang-common analyzer capability could bottleneck.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A Laravel fixture with `class UserController extends Controller { function show($id) { return view('users.show', ['user' => ...]); } }` and `resources/views/users/show.blade.php` produces a `renders` edge.\n- Dotted view names map to nested directories.\n- 100% coverage on changed source."  # bbe5
